{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"## Conclusion\n\nThe supplied data do **not support a positive gain effect in vmPFC** for the equal-indifference group. The mean vmPFC estimate was −0.0036 map units (95% CI −0.0285 to 0.0212; one-sided *p* = .615; *n* = 54). No whole-brain FWE-significant voxels overlapped the anatomical vmPFC mask.\n\nThe one-sided whole-brain test used voxelwise Bonferroni correction, as required by the [NARPS Hypothesis 1 instructions](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf). It found 11 significant voxels in three small posterior occipital foci, outside vmPFC. This is not evidence for the target hypothesis. The null vmPFC result does not prove absence of a response or establish equivalence to zero.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- [Scientific report](</Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/workspaces/narps-neutral-r1-02/report.md>)\n- [Analysis code](</Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/workspaces/narps-neutral-r1-02/analysis/group_analysis.py>)\n- [Statistical summary](</Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/workspaces/narps-neutral-r1-02/results/summary.json>)\n- [Whole-brain focus coordinates](</Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/workspaces/narps-neutral-r1-02/results/wholebrain_fwe_clusters.tsv>)\n- [Mean effect and vmPFC mask figure](</Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/workspaces/narps-neutral-r1-02/figures/mean_effect_vmPFC.png>)\n- [Whole-brain corrected results figure](</Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/workspaces/narps-neutral-r1-02/figures/wholebrain_fwe.png>)\n\nAll 54 participants were included, and the input map checksums were verified. The report discusses the upstream-model, atlas, and group-inference limitations, including why these effect estimates cannot be interpreted per currency unit."}}
